window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Death sucks.</b></p> <p>Are you still considered an orphan if you’re twenty-five years old? Because I am in every sense of the word. I have no one left. No one to love me. No one to care about me. No one to be proud of me.<br> <br> Pulling myself out of a year-long pity party is exhausting, but I slowly start to put the broken pieces of my heart back together and move on.</p> <p>That is until three stupidly attractive men walk into my bar and fast-track everything. When I’m presented with the opportunity to spend the night with them, I decided to take life by the balls and jump head first. <i>Cause why not…right?</i></p> <p>Who knew that one night with them was going to change my whole life…and maybe not for the better.</p> <p><i>This is a contemporary romance with a little suspense where the girl will end up with multiple love interests; all of the characters are in their mid to late twenties. This book ends on a cliffhanger. Royal is part of a duet that is in </i><b><i>The Crown series.</i></b><i> **Trigger Warning: this book features cancer loss, depression, violence, kidnapping, and multiple attempts to unalive someone.</i></p>"; 
